{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177245-2e-core-sorcery-vs-blood-sorcery-book","id":1177245,"title":"[2E] Core Sorcery Vs Blood Sorcery book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-19T05:51:08-08:00","id":1177245,"title":"[2E] Core Sorcery Vs Blood Sorcery book","content":"So i am preparing for a Requiem campaign in t he near future so I am deciding on rules and one thing that I am struggling with is Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> I am curious if anyone has any experience using the Blood Sorcery from the Book &quot;Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies&quot; in Requiem 2nd and how it went? I am tempted to use that system as it seems more open than the one in the Core.<br /> <br /> However as a side note something that keeps bugging me is the casting time. Its seems that casting 15 minutes to get a whip make the weapon non-viable for combat. I guess i can rule out if i use blood sorcery (from the supplement) that some rituals have instant casting time or something.<br /> <br /> On The blood Sorcery supplement something that is not very clear is the sacrifice required for Theban sorcery. Cruac is very simple, X effect required Y amount of Vitae but nothing on what kind sacrifices Theban requires.<br /> <br /> So any experience using blood sorcery of Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies or using things like Blood Scourge in combat with the Core books sorcery? <br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 01-19-2018, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T06:41:06-08:00","id":1177258,"title":"","content":"Well, I know that Sacraments and Blasphemy is a 1e requiem book, so I know there are some differences between some of the rules. The rituals in the book itself should be fine when using 2e though because the book's rules were used in designing 2e rites, if memory serves.<br /> <br /> I've had the book used in games I have played, and in general I prefer having singular rites over the ritual themes; it's mostly a case of less book keeping for me, and the fact I didn't like the idea of being stuck with one theme of rituals.<br /> <br /> On the casting time of blood sorcery, in first edition it was usually an instant action, and that made it a far better option than most other disciplines. So I believe the fifteen minute intervals were for some balance purposes. Some of the rituals were affected by this, others not so much (Touch of the Morrigan comes to mind, what with it usually doing one lethal whenever I use it). I'd suggest checking out the 2e Secrets of the Covenants book if you end up keeping the 15 minute intervals, seeing as the rituals in there seem to be a bit more useful considering the length of time they will take.<br /> <br /> Theban Sorcery usually requires a physical sacrifice of some sort. I suggest checking the pre-written Theban miracles to get an idea what they're all about.<br /> <br /> In my experience, at least for 2e, Blood Sorcery is useless in terms of unprepared combat. With a couple hours of preparation, blood sorcery becomes infinitely more useful for combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T07:37:33-08:00","id":1177276,"title":"","content":"I used Blood Sorcery in my year-long 2nd edition game. I had to teak a few things and in fact I was writting down a sort of 2nd ed update. I didn't have a problem with magic not being used on the spot, as far as I am concerned instant magic effects are the purview of Disciplines, but even with Sorcery you have work arounds like having a latent ritual be activated later.<br /> <br /> EDIT: as for sacramant requirements of Theban Sorcery, a good rule of thumb is something with an Availability of half the dots needed for the Ritual rounded up (so Availability 1 for 1 or 2 dots, 2 for 3-4 and 3 for a 5 dot Ritual) at minumum, you can require something more expensive/hard to get if the Ritual is particularly potent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 01-19-2018, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T08:59:12-08:00","id":1177314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177245-2e-core-sorcery-vs-blood-sorcery-book?p=1177276#post1177276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used Blood Sorcery in my year-long 2nd edition game. I had to teak a few things and in fact I was writting down a sort of 2nd ed update. I didn't have a problem with magic not being used on the spot, as far as I am concerned instant magic effects are the purview of Disciplines,</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont have a problem with blood magic making disciplines less as things like the Blood whip are useless with 2E casting times and i allow the coil of zinitra + Pyrokinesis so my games tend to be &quot;Masquerade-esque lets kill a bunch of shovel heads&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177245-2e-core-sorcery-vs-blood-sorcery-book?p=1177276#post1177276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but even with Sorcery you have work arounds like having a latent ritual be activated later.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177245-2e-core-sorcery-vs-blood-sorcery-book?p=1177276#post1177276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: as for sacramant requirements of Theban Sorcery, a good rule of thumb is something with an Availability of half the dots needed for the Ritual rounded up (so Availability 1 for 1 or 2 dots, 2 for 3-4 and 3 for a 5 dot Ritual) at minumum, you can require something more expensive/hard to get if the Ritual is particularly potent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the guideline <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:26:47-08:00","id":1177326,"title":"","content":"If I were to be honest, the casting times for Blood Sorcery have always been kinda bunk, because &quot;rituals that take at least 10 minutes per casting interval&quot; doesn't work for every spell, and &quot;rituals that take one turn per casting interval&quot; doesn't work for every spell either; this was an issue since first edition with spells like the one that makes a blood whip and other magic that should have been combat applicable on demand, and it's still present in the 2e core book.<br /> <br /> The exploitable creative thaumaturgy rules in the Blood Sorcery book didn't help square this circle, since the amount of improvisation and flexibility it opened up contributed to the opposite of consistency, and arguably flipped the rules paradigm around into a shape that clashes heavily with the mystical assumptions it should have had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T11:48:16-08:00","id":1177374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can do that? </div> </div> </div>Using the Blood Sorcery rules at least. You can add a Divination 2 component to any spell to hold it to be released later by a trigger, so you can prepare a spell before hand, set an activation action or word and use it on the spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T12:09:06-08:00","id":1177379,"title":"","content":"In the 2e requiem book, a lot of the combat spells can be held till sunrise. Like with blood scourge, the kindred can choose at any point in the night for it to activate. If a Kindred had a reliable source of willpower refreshment (in a lot of vampire games i'be played willpower can be scarce), they could use blood scourge once a night if they're feeling paranoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T14:07:33-08:00","id":1177410,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, you can cast the ritual previously, for instance when you awake, but not summon the whip. If later, yoy're in combat, you can summon the whip reflexively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 01-20-2018, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}